<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::strike_rate" target="iran_gulf_flashpoint::crude_throughput_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained spike in cross‑border missile and drone strikes raises insurance premiums and perceived transit risk for global shipping, prompting tanker operators to reroute or idle vessels and insurers to restrict cover for certain Gulf transits, which lowers crude throughput through key chokepoints.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_flashpoint</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::strike_rate" target="tech_ai_superpower_rival::model_dev_velocity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher strike rates create acute operational demands (targeting, ISR, EW) and rich real-world data/feedback that drive defense labs and contractors to shorten iteration cycles and prioritize rapid model improvements, accelerating development velocity for relevant capabilities.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">tech_ai_superpower_rival</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::strike_rate" target="us_treasury_bond_crisis::market_stress_level" id="0">
