  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained increases in defensive materiel resupply funded by Western governments raise expected Treasury issuance or Treasury/Fed support needs, prompting higher rates of long‑maturity bond purchases or other yield‑smoothing interventions to absorb supply and cap yields.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_treasury_bond_crisis</data>
</edge>
