<edge source="iran_gulf_flashpoint::sec_pressure_effect" target="russia_ukraine_war::air_defence_effect" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">More effective extraterritorial/secondary pressure constrains suppliers and maintenance providers for Western-made radars, sensors and spare parts, degrading operational performance and readiness rates of deployed air‑defence systems in the Ukraine theatre within procurement and repair cycles.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_flashpoint</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_flashpoint::sec_pressure_effect" target="tech_ai_superpower_rival::ai_hardware_supply" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">More effective extraterritorial/secondary measures force component suppliers, logistics firms and banks to cut or block shipments to sanctioned intermediaries and their ecosystems, directly reducing the volume of AI accelerators and boards that reach global markets.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_flashpoint</data>
  <data key="d39">tech_ai_superpower_rival</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_flashpoint::sec_pressure_effect" target="us_canada_trade_war::retaliation_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">An increase in the effectiveness of extraterritorial/secondary pressure on third‑party firms pushes the targeted government (or its trading partners) to accelerate reciprocal trade measures to shield domestic companies and signal political resistance.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_flashpoint</data>
  <data key="d39">us_canada_trade_war</data>
</edge>
