<edge source="iran_gulf_flashpoint::trade_finance_avail" target="russia_ukraine_war::resupply_rate_defense" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Reduced availability of trade finance and letters of credit directly delays or cancels payments for interceptors, munitions and contracted deliveries, slowing the flow rate of defensive materiel into the Ukrainian operational theatre.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_flashpoint</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_flashpoint::trade_finance_avail" target="tech_ai_superpower_rival::ai_capital_inflows" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A tightening of trade finance and correspondent banking for affected trade lanes raises transaction costs and payment risk for cross‑border deals, causing investors and foreign corporate buyers to delay or withhold capital allocations into AI hardware manufacturing and startups that rely on those imports.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_flashpoint</data>
  <data key="d39">tech_ai_superpower_rival</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_flashpoint::trade_finance_avail" target="us_canada_trade_war::supply_reconfig_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A drop in availability of trade finance for shipments tied to the Gulf prompt firms to speed up re‑sourcing and relocating production to jurisdictions with more reliable payment/credit channels, raising the observed reconfiguration rate (and conversely, higher availability slows reconfiguration).</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_flashpoint</data>
  <data key="d39">us_canada_trade_war</data>
</edge>
