<edge source="us_treasury_bond_crisis::market_stress_level" target="iran_gulf_flashpoint::trade_finance_avail" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Acute stress in the US Treasury market causes global banks to hoard liquidity and cut non‑core, higher‑risk correspondent and trade‑finance lines (including those that historically dealt indirectly with Iran), directly reducing the availability of letters of credit and correspondent services for Iranian trade.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_treasury_bond_crisis</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_flashpoint</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_treasury_bond_crisis::market_stress_level" target="iran_gulf_flashpoint::sec_pressure_effect" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Systemic bond‑market stress triggers rapid de‑risking by international banks and corporates who seek to avoid any exposures that could attract regulatory scrutiny, thereby making US extraterritorial/secondary measures more effective in curtailing third‑party dealings with Iran.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_treasury_bond_crisis</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_flashpoint</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_treasury_bond_crisis::market_stress_level" target="russia_ukraine_war::logistics_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Acute bond-market stress forces banks and freight financiers to pull or sharply re-price trade-finance, letters of credit and insurance, directly constraining commercial shipping, maintenance and transport throughput that sustain military and civilian materiel flows.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_treasury_bond_crisis</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_treasury_bond_crisis::market_stress_level" target="tech_ai_superpower_rival::ai_hardware_supply" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Acute stress in the bond market tightens short-term financing and triggers margin calls for suppliers and distributors, forcing producers to delay shipments or cut production of AI accelerators and boards due to working-capital shortages.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_treasury_bond_crisis</data>
  <data key="d39">tech_ai_superpower_rival</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_treasury_bond_crisis::market_stress_level" target="us_canada_trade_war::bilateral_trade_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Acute bond‑market stress tightens short‑term funding and trade‑finance lines and forces firms to delay shipments and cut orders, producing an immediate drop in cross‑border goods and services volumes between the two countries.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_treasury_bond_crisis</data>
  <data key="d39">us_canada_trade_war</data>
</edge>
